/-!
# Subformations of the formation generated by a group (Kourovka Notebook Problem 16.31)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 16.31 (V. A. Vedernikov): suppose that a
group `G` has a composition series and let `𝔉(G)` be the formation generated by `G`. Is the set of
all subformations of `𝔉(G)` finite?

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 16.31 (V. A.
Vedernikov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00701223 (`KOU-16.31`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Stated for finite `G`, where the Archive's counterexample lives, so the refutation is the stronger
statement. Formations are classes of finite groups in `Type` closed under homomorphic images and
finite subdirect products (`G / N₁, G / N₂ ∈ 𝔉` implies `G / (N₁ ∩ N₂) ∈ 𝔉`). A class is a predicate
on finite groups; closure under homomorphic images makes it closed under isomorphism, so distinct
formations are distinct predicates. The formation generated by `G` is the intersection of all
formations containing `G`.

We prove `finitelyManySubformations_refuted` using the regular wreath product
$T = \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbf F_5) \wr C_2$. For each $n$, take the subgroup of $T^{\mathbf F_2^n}$
whose projections to $C_2$ form an affine function on the cube. Quotient by the central sign
vectors of even weight to obtain a finite group $H_n$ in the formation generated by $T$.

To separate $H_n$ from $H_m$ for $m > n$, prescribe central values of free group words under
finitely many epimorphisms onto $T$. The prescribed sign is the product of the swap indicators of
$n$ marked words. The sum of a product of $n$ affine functions on an $m$-dimensional cube vanishes
when $m > n$. On the $n$-dimensional cube, the product of the coordinate functions has sum one.
This gives a formation containing $H_m$ and excluding $H_n$.

The formation predicate `IsFormation` has the same body as the one used for the lattice of
formations (Kourovka Problem 13.51); `isFormation_iff_isFormation` records this.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FormationSubformationsFiniteKourovka16Problem31Wanted

/-- **Classes of finite groups.** A class of finite groups is a predicate on finite groups: it
assigns to every finite group $G$ a proposition, read as "$G$ belongs to the class". The class need
not be closed under isomorphism. -/
abbrev FiniteGroupClass : Type 1 :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G], Prop

/-- **Formations of finite groups, possibly empty.** A class $\mathfrak{F}$ of finite groups is a
formation if it is closed under homomorphic images (whenever $f \colon G \to H$ is a surjective
homomorphism of finite groups and $G \in \mathfrak{F}$, then $H \in \mathfrak{F}$) and under finite
subdirect products (whenever $N_1$ and $N_2$ are normal subgroups of a finite group $G$ with
$G / N_1 \in \mathfrak{F}$ and $G / N_2 \in \mathfrak{F}$, then
$G / (N_1 \cap N_2) \in \mathfrak{F}$). In particular the empty class is a formation. -/
def IsFormation (F : FiniteGroupClass) : Prop :=
  (∀ (G H : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] [Group H] [Finite H] (f : G →* H),
      Function.Surjective f → F G → F H) ∧
    ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] (N₁ N₂ : Subgroup G) [N₁.Normal] [N₂.Normal],
      F (G ⧸ N₁) → F (G ⧸ N₂) → F (G ⧸ (N₁ ⊓ N₂))

/-- **Formation generated by a finite group.** For a finite group $G$, the formation generated by
$G$ is the class of finite groups $H$ such that $H$ belongs to every formation that contains $G$;
that is, it is the intersection of all formations containing $G$. -/
def formationGeneratedBy (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] : FiniteGroupClass :=
  fun (H : Type) [Group H] [Finite H] => ∀ F : FiniteGroupClass, IsFormation F → F G → F H

/-- **Kourovka Problem 16.31 for finite groups.** The statement (V. A. Vedernikov) that for every
finite group $G$ only finitely many formations of finite groups are contained in the formation
generated by $G$. Here formations may be empty, and a formation $\mathfrak{F}$ is contained in the
formation generated by $G$ when every finite group in $\mathfrak{F}$ belongs to the formation
generated by $G$. -/
def finitelyManySubformations : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G],
    {F : FiniteGroupClass | IsFormation F ∧
      ∀ (H : Type) [Group H] [Finite H], F H → formationGeneratedBy G H}.Finite

/-- **Two definitions of formations agree.** A class $\mathfrak{F}$ of finite groups is a
formation in the sense used for Kourovka Problem 16.31 if and only if it is a formation in the
sense used for the lattice of formations in Kourovka Problem 13.51: both definitions ask for
closure under homomorphic images and under finite subdirect products, with the same clauses.

Source: unfolding the two definitions, which have the same body. -/
theorem isFormation_iff_isFormation (F : FiniteGroupClass) :
    IsFormation F ↔ FiniteModularLatticeFormationsKourovka13Problem51Wanted.IsFormation F :=
  Iff.rfl

open Function
open scoped BigOperators MatrixGroups

/- Intersect the kernels one coordinate at a time to obtain a finite subdirect power. -/
private theorem subdirect_mem (G H : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] [Group H] [Finite H]
    {ι : Type} [Finite ι] (f : ι → H →* G) (hf : ∀ i, Surjective (f i))
    (hmono : ∀ x, (∀ i, f i x = 1) → x = 1) : formationGeneratedBy G H := by
  classical
  let := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  intro F hF hG
  let P (N : Subgroup H) := ∃ _ : N.Normal, F (H ⧸ N)
  have aux (s : Finset ι) : P (s.inf (fun i ↦ (f i).ker)) := by
    induction s using Finset.induction_on with
    | empty =>
      simp only [Finset.inf_empty]
      change ∃ _ : (⊤ : Subgroup H).Normal, F (H ⧸ (⊤ : Subgroup H))
      have := QuotientGroup.subsingleton_quotient_top (G := H)
      exact ⟨inferInstance, hF.1 G _ 1 (fun x ↦ ⟨1, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩) hG⟩
    | insert i s _ ih =>
      simp only [Finset.inf_insert]
      obtain ⟨hN, hmem⟩ := ih
      let e := QuotientGroup.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (f i) (hf i)
      exact ⟨inferInstance, hF.2 H _ _ (hF.1 _ _ e.symm.toMonoidHom e.symm.surjective hG) hmem⟩
  obtain ⟨hN, hmem⟩ := aux Finset.univ
  have heq : Finset.univ.inf (fun i ↦ (f i).ker) = ⊥ := by
    apply eq_bot_iff.mpr
    intro x hx
    apply hmono
    intro i
    exact Finset.inf_le (f := fun j ↦ (f j).ker) (Finset.mem_univ i) hx
  let e := (QuotientGroup.quotientMulEquivOfEq heq).trans QuotientGroup.quotientBot
  exact hF.1 _ _ e.toMonoidHom e.surjective hmem

private abbrev F₂ := ZMod 2
private abbrev C₂ := Multiplicative F₂
private abbrev Cube (n : ℕ) := Fin n → F₂
private abbrev SL₂ := SL(2, ZMod 5)
private abbrev Wreath := SL₂ ≀ᵣ C₂
private def sign (t : Wreath) : F₂ := t.right.toAdd

/- The right component of a wreath product element records whether it swaps the two factors.
Only this component is constrained as the point of the cube varies. -/
private def affineSubgroup (n : ℕ) : Subgroup (Cube n → Wreath) where
  carrier := {f | ∃ (c : F₂) (l : Cube n →+ F₂), ∀ x, sign (f x) = c + l x}
  one_mem' := ⟨0, 0, fun _ ↦ by simp [sign]⟩
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro f g ⟨a, l, hf⟩ ⟨b, k, hg⟩
    refine ⟨a + b, l + k, fun x ↦ ?_⟩
    change sign (f x) + sign (g x) = _
    rw [hf, hg]
    simp only [AddMonoidHom.add_apply]
    abel
  inv_mem' := by
    rintro f ⟨c, l, hf⟩
    exact ⟨-c, -l, fun x ↦ by change -sign (f x) = _; simp [hf, add_comm]⟩

private def coord (n : ℕ) (x : Cube n) : affineSubgroup n →* Wreath :=
  (Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun _ : Cube n ↦ Wreath) x).comp (affineSubgroup n).subtype

private theorem coord_surjective (n : ℕ) (x : Cube n) : Surjective (coord n x) := by
  intro t
  exact ⟨⟨fun _ ↦ t, sign t, 0, fun _ ↦ (add_zero _).symm⟩, rfl⟩

private theorem affineSubgroup_mem (n : ℕ) : formationGeneratedBy Wreath (affineSubgroup n) := by
  apply subdirect_mem Wreath (affineSubgroup n) (coord n) (coord_surjective n)
  intro u h
  exact Subtype.ext (funext h)

private def centralBit (b : F₂) : SL₂ := if b = 0 then 1 else -1
private def centralElt (b : F₂) : Wreath := ⟨fun _ ↦ centralBit b, 1⟩

private theorem centralElt_zero : centralElt 0 = 1 := by
  rfl

private theorem centralElt_add (a b : F₂) : centralElt (a + b) = centralElt a * centralElt b := by
  apply RegularWreathProduct.ext
  · funext i
    change centralBit (a + b) = centralBit a * centralBit b
    have casesB : ∀ t : F₂, t = 0 ∨ t = 1 := by decide
    rcases casesB a with rfl | rfl <;> rcases casesB b with rfl | rfl <;>
      simp [centralBit, ZModModule.add_self]
  · rfl

private theorem centralElt_injective : Injective centralElt := by
  intro a b h
  have he := congrArg (fun t : Wreath ↦ ((t.left 1 : SL₂) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) (ZMod 5)) 0 0) h
  fin_cases a <;> fin_cases b <;> first | rfl | exact False.elim (by revert he; decide)

private theorem centralElt_commute (a : F₂) (t : Wreath) : Commute (centralElt a) t := by
  apply RegularWreathProduct.ext
  · funext i
    change centralBit a * t.left ((1 : C₂)⁻¹ * i) = t.left i * centralBit a
    simp only [inv_one, one_mul, centralBit]
    split <;> simp
  · simp [centralElt]

/- In this central subgroup, a sign at each vertex represents the same involution in both
wreath factors, and the total number of negative signs is even. -/
private def evenCenter (n : ℕ) : Subgroup (affineSubgroup n) where
  carrier := {u | ∃ a : Cube n → F₂, ∑ i, a i = 0 ∧ ∀ i, u.val i = centralElt (a i)}
  one_mem' := ⟨0, by simp, fun _ ↦ centralElt_zero.symm⟩
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro u v ⟨a, ha, hu⟩ ⟨b, hb, hv⟩
    exact ⟨a + b, by simp [Finset.sum_add_distrib, ha, hb],
      fun i ↦ by change u.val i * v.val i = _; rw [hu, hv, Pi.add_apply, centralElt_add]⟩
  inv_mem' := by
    rintro u ⟨a, ha, hu⟩
    refine ⟨-a, by simp [ha], fun i ↦ ?_⟩
    change (u.val i)⁻¹ = centralElt (-(a i))
    apply inv_eq_of_mul_eq_one_right
    rw [hu, ← centralElt_add, add_neg_cancel, centralElt_zero]

private instance evenCenterNormal (n : ℕ) : (evenCenter n).Normal :=
  Subgroup.normal_of_le_center (by
    rintro u ⟨a, _, hu⟩
    apply Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mpr
    intro v
    apply Subtype.ext
    funext i
    change v.val i * u.val i = u.val i * v.val i
    rw [hu]
    exact (centralElt_commute _ _).eq.symm)

private abbrev parityQuotient (n : ℕ) := affineSubgroup n ⧸ evenCenter n

private theorem parityQuotient_mem (n : ℕ) : formationGeneratedBy Wreath (parityQuotient n) := by
  intro F hF hT
  exact hF.1 _ _ (QuotientGroup.mk' _) (QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective _)
    (affineSubgroup_mem n F hF hT)

/- Translation by a nonzero common kernel vector pairs vertices with the same summand. -/
private theorem sum_affine_products_eq_zero {n m : ℕ} (hnm : n < m) (c : Fin n → F₂)
    (l : Fin n → (Cube m →+ F₂)) : ∑ x : Cube m, ∏ i, (c i + l i x) = 0 := by
  classical
  let f : Cube m → Cube n := fun x i ↦ l i x
  have hc : Fintype.card (Cube n) < Fintype.card (Cube m) := by
    simpa [Cube, F₂, Fintype.card_fun] using
      (Nat.pow_lt_pow_right (by decide : 1 < 2) hnm)
  obtain ⟨x, y, hxy, hne⟩ := Function.not_injective_iff.mp
    (Fintype.not_injective_of_card_lt f hc)
  let k := x - y
  have hk : k ≠ 0 := sub_ne_zero.mpr hne
  have hl (i : Fin n) : l i k = 0 := by
    simpa only [k, map_sub, sub_eq_zero] using congrFun hxy i
  apply Finset.sum_ninvolution (fun v ↦ v + k)
  · intro v
    simp [hl, ZModModule.add_self]
  · intro v _
    simpa using hk
  · simp
  · intro v
    simp [add_assoc, ZModModule.add_self]

private abbrev Words := FreeGroup ℕ
/- Use epimorphisms from the free group that send all sufficiently late generators to one.
These unused generators can cover the kernel when lifting an epimorphism of finite groups. -/
private def Admissible {K : Type} [Group K] (h : Words →* K) :=
  Surjective h ∧ ∃ n : ℕ, ∀ i ≥ n, h (FreeGroup.of i) = 1

private theorem finite_enumeration (K : Type) [Group K] [Finite K] :
    ∃ v : ℕ → K, Surjective v ∧ ∃ n, ∀ i ≥ n, v i = 1 := by
  classical
  let := Fintype.ofFinite K
  let e := Fintype.equivFin K
  refine ⟨fun i ↦ if h : i < Fintype.card K then e.symm ⟨i, h⟩ else 1, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro k
    exact ⟨(e k).val, by simp [(e k).isLt]⟩
  · exact ⟨Fintype.card K, fun i hi ↦ by simp [not_lt.mpr hi]⟩

private theorem admissible_comp {H K : Type} [Group H] [Group K] {h : Words →* H}
    (hh : Admissible h) (q : H →* K) (hq : Surjective q) : Admissible (q.comp h) := by
  obtain ⟨hs, n, hn⟩ := hh
  exact ⟨hq.comp hs, n, fun i hi ↦ by simp [hn i hi]⟩

private theorem admissible_lift {H K : Type} [Group H] [Finite H] [Group K] [Finite K]
    (q : H →* K) (hq : Surjective q) {h : Words →* K} (hh : Admissible h) :
    ∃ t : Words →* H, Admissible t ∧ q.comp t = h := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨hs, n, hn⟩ := hh
  obtain ⟨v, hv, m, hm⟩ := finite_enumeration q.ker
  choose sectionMap hsection using hq
  let t := FreeGroup.lift (fun i ↦ if i < n then sectionMap (h (.of i)) else (v (i - n)).val)
  have qt : q.comp t = h := by
    apply FreeGroup.ext_hom
    intro i
    change q (t (.of i)) = _
    simp only [t, FreeGroup.lift_apply_of]
    split
    · apply hsection
    · rename_i hi
      rw [hn _ (Nat.le_of_not_gt hi)]
      exact (v _).property
  have hk (a : H) (ha : a ∈ q.ker) : a ∈ t.range := by
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hv ⟨a, ha⟩
    exact ⟨.of (n + i), by simp [t, hi]⟩
  refine ⟨t, ⟨?_, n + m, ?_⟩, qt⟩
  · intro y
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hs (q y)
    have hqw : q (t w) = q y := (DFunLike.congr_fun qt w).trans hw
    have hy : y / t w ∈ t.range := hk _ (by simp [MonoidHom.mem_ker, hqw])
    exact show y ∈ t.range from by simpa using t.range.mul_mem hy (show t w ∈ t.range from ⟨w, rfl⟩)
  · intro i hi
    simp [t, show ¬i < n by omega, hm (i - n) (by omega)]

private theorem exists_admissible (K : Type) [Group K] [Finite K] :
    ∃ h : Words →* K, Admissible h := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv, m, hm⟩ := finite_enumeration K
  exact ⟨FreeGroup.lift v, FreeGroup.lift_surjective_of_surjective hv, m,
    fun i hi ↦ by simpa using hm i hi⟩

private abbrev Epi (T : Type) [Group T] := {f : Words →* T // Surjective f}

private def constraints {T : Type} [Group T] (value : Epi T → T)
    (t : Finset (Epi T)) (w : Words) := ∀ q ∈ t, q.val w = value q

/- Under each admissible epimorphism, some finite collection of the prescribed word values
forces the word into the kernel. Collections for two quotients can be combined by union. -/
private def wordClass {T : Type} [Group T] (value : Epi T → T) : FiniteGroupClass :=
  fun H _ _ ↦ ∀ f : Words →* H, Admissible f →
    ∃ t : Finset (Epi T), ∀ w, constraints value t w → f w = 1

private theorem wordClass_formation {T : Type} [Group T] (value : Epi T → T) :
    IsFormation (wordClass value) := by
  classical
  constructor
  · intro G H _ _ _ _ q hq hG f hf
    obtain ⟨t, ht, hqt⟩ := admissible_lift q hq hf
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hG t ht
    exact ⟨s, fun w hw ↦ by rw [← hqt, MonoidHom.comp_apply, hs w hw, map_one]⟩
  · intro G _ _ N M _ _ hN hM f hf
    let p {K : Subgroup G} [K.Normal] (h : N ⊓ M ≤ K) :=
      QuotientGroup.map (N ⊓ M) K (MonoidHom.id G) h
    have ps {K : Subgroup G} [K.Normal] (h : N ⊓ M ≤ K) : Surjective (p h) :=
      QuotientGroup.map_surjective_of_surjective (N ⊓ M) K (MonoidHom.id G)
        (QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective K) h
    obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hN _ (admissible_comp hf _ (ps inf_le_left))
    obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := hM _ (admissible_comp hf _ (ps inf_le_right))
    refine ⟨u ∪ v, fun w hw ↦ ?_⟩
    have h₁ := hu w (fun q hq ↦ hw q (Finset.mem_union_left _ hq))
    have h₂ := hv w (fun q hq ↦ hw q (Finset.mem_union_right _ hq))
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective (N ⊓ M) (f w)
    change p inf_le_left (f w) = 1 at h₁
    change p inf_le_right (f w) = 1 at h₂
    rw [← hg] at h₁ h₂ ⊢
    exact (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).2
      ⟨(QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).1 h₁, (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).1 h₂⟩

/- Epimorphisms to a fixed finite simple group have incomparable distinct kernels.
Perfectness then lets one prescribe values independently across finitely many distinct kernels. -/
private theorem map_other_ker {X P : Type} [Group X] [Group P] [Finite P] [IsSimpleGroup P]
    {f g : X →* P} (hf : Surjective f) (hg : Surjective g) (hne : f.ker ≠ g.ker) :
    g.ker.map f = ⊤ := by
  have := Subgroup.Normal.map (H := g.ker) inferInstance f hf
  apply (Subgroup.Normal.eq_bot_or_eq_top (g.ker.map f)).resolve_left
  intro h
  have hlt := lt_of_le_of_ne ((Subgroup.map_eq_bot_iff _).mp h) (Ne.symm hne)
  have := Subgroup.index_strictAnti hlt
  simp [Subgroup.index_ker, f.range_eq_top_of_surjective hf,
    g.range_eq_top_of_surjective hg] at this

private theorem map_inf_kernels {X P ι : Type} [Group X] [Group P] [Finite P] [IsSimpleGroup P]
    [Group.IsPerfect P] (f : ι → X →* P) (hf : ∀ i, Surjective (f i))
    (i : ι) (s : Finset ι) (hne : ∀ j ∈ s, (f i).ker ≠ (f j).ker) :
    (s.inf fun j ↦ (f j).ker).map (f i) = ⊤ := by
  classical
  have norms (t : Finset ι) : (t.inf fun j ↦ (f j).ker).Normal := by
    induction t using Finset.induction_on with
    | empty => simp
    | insert j t _ h => rw [Finset.inf_insert]; infer_instance
  induction s using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => simpa only [Finset.inf_empty] using Subgroup.map_top_of_surjective (f i) (hf i)
  | insert j s _ ih =>
    rw [Finset.inf_insert]
    have := norms s
    have hcomm := Subgroup.map_mono (f := f i) (Subgroup.commutator_le_inf
      (H₁ := (f j).ker) (H₂ := s.inf fun a ↦ (f a).ker))
    rw [Subgroup.map_commutator,
      map_other_ker (hf i) (hf j) (hne _ (Finset.mem_insert_self ..)),
      ih (fun a ha ↦ hne a (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem ha)),
      ← commutator_def, Group.IsPerfect.commutator_eq_top] at hcomm
    exact top_unique hcomm

private theorem prescribe_involutions {X P ι : Type} [Group X] [Group P] [Finite P]
    [IsSimpleGroup P] [Group.IsPerfect P] (f : ι → X →* P) (hf : ∀ i, Surjective (f i))
    (enabled : ι → Prop) (hc : ∀ i j, (f i).ker = (f j).ker → (enabled i ↔ enabled j))
    (a : P) (ha : a ≠ 1) (ha2 : a ^ 2 = 1) (s : Finset ι) :
    ∃ x : X, ∀ i ∈ s, x ^ 2 ∈ (f i).ker ∧ (x ∈ (f i).ker ↔ ¬ enabled i) := by
  classical
  induction s using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => simp
  | insert i s _ ih =>
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := ih
    by_cases h : ∃ j ∈ s, (f i).ker = (f j).ker
    · obtain ⟨j, hj, he⟩ := h
      refine ⟨x, (Finset.forall_mem_insert _ _ _).mpr ⟨?_, hx⟩⟩
      simpa only [he, hc i j he] using hx j hj
    · push Not at h
      let y := if enabled i then a else 1
      have ht := map_inf_kernels f hf i s h
      obtain ⟨z, hz, hz'⟩ := (show y / f i x ∈ (s.inf fun j ↦ (f j).ker).map (f i) by
        rw [ht]; exact Subgroup.mem_top _)
      have hi : f i (z * x) = y := by simp [hz']
      refine ⟨z * x, (Finset.forall_mem_insert _ _ _).mpr ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩
      · simp only [MonoidHom.mem_ker, map_pow, hi]
        by_cases e : enabled i <;> simp [y, e, ha, ha2]
      · intro j hj
        have hjz : f j z = 1 := Finset.inf_le (f := fun j ↦ (f j).ker) hj hz
        simpa [MonoidHom.mem_ker, hjz] using hx j hj

private abbrev PSL₂ := PSL(2, ZMod 5)
private abbrev project : SL₂ →* PSL₂ := QuotientGroup.mk' (Subgroup.center SL₂)

private instance primeFive : Fact (Nat.Prime 5) := ⟨by decide⟩

private instance simplePSL : IsSimpleGroup PSL₂ :=
  Matrix.ProjectiveSpecialLinearGroup.rank_two_simple (F := ZMod 5) (by simp)

private instance perfectSL : Group.IsPerfect SL₂ :=
  ⟨Matrix.SL2.commutator_eq_top (a := (2 : ZMod 5)) (by decide) (by decide)⟩

/- A lift of the identity of PSL₂(5) squares to I. A lift of an involution squares to −I. -/
private theorem central_cases {a : SL₂} (ha : project a = 1) : a = 1 ∨ a = -1 := by
  obtain ⟨r, hr, hmat⟩ :=
    Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.mem_center_iff.mp ((QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).mp ha)
  have h : r ^ 2 = 1 := by simpa using hr
  rcases sq_eq_one_iff.mp h with rfl | rfl
  · left
    exact Subtype.ext (by simpa using hmat.symm)
  · right
    apply Subtype.ext
    rw [← hmat]
    ext i j
    fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> decide

private theorem sq_one_central {a : SL₂} (ha : a ^ 2 = 1) : project a = 1 := by
  have hinv : a = a⁻¹ := eq_inv_of_mul_eq_one_left (by simpa [pow_two] using ha)
  have entries (i j : Fin 2) := congrArg (fun b : SL₂ ↦ b.val i j) hinv
  simp only [Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.coe_inv, Matrix.adjugate_fin_two] at entries
  have neg_eq_zero : ∀ t : ZMod 5, t = -t → t = 0 := by decide
  have h01 : a.val 0 1 = 0 := neg_eq_zero _ (entries 0 1)
  have h10 : a.val 1 0 = 0 := neg_eq_zero _ (entries 1 0)
  have hdiag : a.val 0 0 = a.val 1 1 := entries 0 0
  have hm : Matrix.scalar (Fin 2) (a.val 0 0) = a.val := by
    ext i j
    fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [Matrix.scalar_apply, h01, h10, hdiag]
  apply (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).mpr
  apply Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mpr
  intro b
  apply Subtype.ext
  change b.val * a.val = a.val * b.val
  exact hm ▸ (Matrix.scalar_commute (a.val 0 0) (Commute.all _) b.val).symm.eq

private theorem central_square {a : SL₂} (ha : project a = 1) : a ^ 2 = 1 := by
  rcases central_cases ha with rfl | rfl <;> simp [pow_two]

private theorem sq_of_project_involution {a : SL₂} (h : project a ^ 2 = 1) (hne : project a ≠ 1) :
    a ^ 2 = -1 := by
  exact (central_cases (a := a ^ 2) (by rwa [map_pow])).resolve_left (hne ∘ sq_one_central)

private theorem exists_involution : ∃ t : PSL₂, t ≠ 1 ∧ t ^ 2 = 1 := by
  let a : SL₂ := Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.map (Int.castRingHom (ZMod 5)) ModularGroup.S
  have ha : a ^ 2 = -1 := by
    apply Subtype.ext
    ext i j
    fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> decide
  refine ⟨project a, fun he ↦ ?_, ?_⟩
  · have he' := (central_square he).symm.trans ha
    exact (by decide : (1 : ZMod 5) ≠ -1) (congrArg (fun b : SL₂ ↦ b.val 0 0) he')
  · rw [← map_pow, ha]
    apply (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).mpr
    exact Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mpr (fun _ ↦ by simp)

private def atBase (i : C₂) : SL₂ →* Wreath where
  toFun a := ⟨fun j ↦ if j = i then a else 1, 1⟩
  map_one' := by ext <;> simp
  map_mul' a b := by
    apply RegularWreathProduct.ext
    · ext j
      simp only [RegularWreathProduct.mul_left, inv_one, one_mul, Pi.mul_apply]
      split <;> simp_all
    · rfl

private theorem base_mem_commutator (i : C₂) (a : SL₂) : atBase i a ∈ commutator Wreath := by
  have h : a ∈ commutator SL₂ := Group.IsPerfect.commutator_eq_top (G := SL₂) ▸ Subgroup.mem_top _
  have hm := Subgroup.mem_map_of_mem (atBase i) h
  rw [map_commutator_eq] at hm
  exact Subgroup.commutator_mono le_top le_top hm

private theorem right_trivial {X : Type} [Group X] (q : X →* Wreath) (x : commutator X) :
    (q x.val).right = 1 :=
  Group.Abelianization.commutator_le_ker (RegularWreathProduct.rightHom.comp q) x.property

private def factorAt {X : Type} [Group X] (q : X →* Wreath) (i : C₂) : commutator X →* SL₂ where
  toFun x := (q x.val).left i
  map_one' := by simp
  map_mul' x y := by simp [right_trivial q x]

private theorem factor_lift {X : Type} [Group X] {q : X →* Wreath} (hq : Surjective q)
    (a : SL₂) (i : C₂) : ∃ x : commutator X, q x.val = atBase i a := by
  have h := base_mem_commutator i a
  rw [← map_commutator_of_surjective hq] at h
  obtain ⟨x, hx, hx'⟩ := h
  exact ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, hx'⟩

private abbrev projectAt {X : Type} [Group X] (q : X →* Wreath) (i : C₂) :=
  project.comp (factorAt q i)

private theorem projectAt_surj {X : Type} [Group X] {q : X →* Wreath} (hq : Surjective q)
    (i : C₂) : Surjective (projectAt q i) := by
  apply (QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective _).comp
  intro a
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := factor_lift hq a i
  exact ⟨x, by simp [factorAt, hx, atBase]⟩

private theorem conj_mem_ker_iff {X : Type} [Group X] (q : X →* Wreath) (g : X) (i : C₂)
    (x : commutator X) :
    MulAut.conjNormal g x ∈ (projectAt q i).ker ↔
      x ∈ (projectAt q ((q g).right⁻¹ * i)).ker := by
  change project ((q (g * x.val * g⁻¹)).left i) = 1 ↔ _
  simp [factorAt, projectAt, MonoidHom.mem_ker, right_trivial q x, ← mul_assoc, conj_eq_one_iff]

/- Conjugation permutes the two projective factor kernels. An element stabilizes either
kernel exactly when it has trivial projection to the swapping group. -/
private theorem stabilizes_iff {X : Type} [Group X] {q : X →* Wreath} (hq : Surjective q)
    (i : C₂) (g : X) : (∀ x : commutator X,
      MulAut.conjNormal g x ∈ (projectAt q i).ker ↔ x ∈ (projectAt q i).ker) ↔ (q g).right = 1 := by
  constructor
  · intro hs
    by_contra hn
    obtain ⟨a, ha, _⟩ := exists_involution
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective (Subgroup.center SL₂) a
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := factor_lift hq b i
    have hne : (q g).right⁻¹ * i ≠ i := by simpa using hn
    have hx₁ : x ∈ (projectAt q ((q g).right⁻¹ * i)).ker := by
      simp [MonoidHom.mem_ker, projectAt, factorAt, hx, atBase, hne]
    have hx₂ := (hs x).mp ((conj_mem_ker_iff q g i x).mpr hx₁)
    apply ha
    rw [← hb]
    exact (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).mpr (by
      simpa [MonoidHom.mem_ker, projectAt, factorAt, hx, atBase] using hx₂)
  · intro hg x
    simpa [hg] using conj_mem_ker_iff q g i x

private theorem sign_of_ker_eq {X : Type} [Group X] {q r : X →* Wreath}
    (hq : Surjective q) (hr : Surjective r) (i j : C₂)
    (he : (projectAt q i).ker = (projectAt r j).ker) (g : X) :
    sign (q g) = sign (r g) := by
  have h : (q g).right = 1 ↔ (r g).right = 1 := by
    rw [← stabilizes_iff hq i g, ← stabilizes_iff hr j g, he]
  change sign (q g) = 0 ↔ sign (r g) = 0 at h
  exact (by decide : ∀ a b : F₂, (a = 0 ↔ b = 0) → a = b) _ _ h

private def swapProduct {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Words) (q : Epi Wreath) : F₂ :=
  ∏ i, sign (q.val (b i))

private def prescribedValue {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Words) (q : Epi Wreath) : Wreath :=
  centralElt (swapProduct b q)

/- In each simple projective factor prescribe the identity or a nontrivial involution.
Equal kernels prescribe the same choice because they detect the same swaps. Squaring a lift
produces the required central sign simultaneously in every coordinate. -/
private theorem realize_constraints {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Words) (s : Finset (Epi Wreath)) :
    ∃ w, constraints (prescribedValue b) s w := by
  classical
  let f (i : s × C₂) := projectAt i.1.val.val i.2
  let enabled (i : s × C₂) := swapProduct b i.1.val ≠ 0
  have hc (i j : s × C₂) (he : (f i).ker = (f j).ker) : enabled i ↔ enabled j := by
    have : swapProduct b i.1.val = swapProduct b j.1.val :=
      Finset.prod_congr rfl (fun k _ ↦ sign_of_ker_eq i.1.val.property j.1.val.property
        i.2 j.2 he (b k))
    change swapProduct b i.1.val ≠ 0 ↔ swapProduct b j.1.val ≠ 0
    rw [this]
  obtain ⟨a, ha, ha2⟩ := exists_involution
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := prescribe_involutions f (fun i ↦ projectAt_surj i.1.val.property i.2)
    enabled hc a ha ha2 Finset.univ
  refine ⟨x.val ^ 2, fun q hq ↦ ?_⟩
  apply RegularWreathProduct.ext
  · funext k
    obtain ⟨hsq, hzero⟩ := hx (⟨q, hq⟩, k) (Finset.mem_univ _)
    rw [MonoidHom.mem_ker, map_pow] at hsq
    change project (factorAt q.val k x) ^ 2 = 1 at hsq
    change project (factorAt q.val k x) = 1 ↔ ¬ swapProduct b q ≠ 0 at hzero
    rw [map_pow, pow_two]
    change (q.val x.val).left k * (q.val x.val).left ((q.val x.val).right⁻¹ * k) = _
    rw [right_trivial q.val x, inv_one, one_mul, ← pow_two]
    change (factorAt q.val k x) ^ 2 = centralBit (swapProduct b q)
    by_cases hw : swapProduct b q = 0
    · simpa [centralBit, hw] using central_square (hzero.mpr (not_not.mpr hw))
    · simpa [centralBit, hw] using sq_of_project_involution hsq (fun h ↦ (hzero.mp h) hw)
  · simp [pow_two, right_trivial q.val x, prescribedValue, centralElt]

/- Lift to the subgroup of functions on the cube. The constraints at all vertices force
a central sign vector whose parity is the sum of a product of affine functions. -/
private theorem largerQuotient_mem {n m : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Words) (hlt : n < m) :
    wordClass (prescribedValue b) (parityQuotient m) := by
  classical
  intro h hh
  let p := QuotientGroup.mk' (evenCenter m)
  obtain ⟨v, hv, hp⟩ := admissible_lift p (QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective _) hh
  let q (x : Cube m) : Epi Wreath := ⟨(coord m x).comp v, (coord_surjective m x).comp hv.1⟩
  refine ⟨Finset.univ.image q, fun w hw ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [← hp]
  apply (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff (v w)).2
  refine ⟨fun x ↦ swapProduct b (q x), ?_,
    fun i ↦ hw _ (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_univ i))⟩
  choose c l hl using fun j ↦ (v (b j)).property
  convert sum_affine_products_eq_zero hlt c l using 1
  apply Finset.sum_congr rfl
  intro x _
  exact Finset.prod_congr rfl (fun j _ ↦ hl j x)

private theorem sum_coordinate_product (n : ℕ) : ∑ x : Cube n, ∏ i, x i = 1 := by
  classical
  rw [Finset.sum_eq_single (1 : Cube n)]
  · simp
  · intro x _ hx
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ : ∃ i, x i ≠ 1 := by
      by_contra! h
      exact hx (funext h)
    exact Finset.prod_eq_zero (Finset.mem_univ i)
      ((by decide : ∀ a : F₂, a ≠ 1 → a = 0) _ hi)
  · simp

/- Mark the coordinate projections on the cube. Their product selects just the all-ones
vertex, so a word realizing the constraints survives the central quotient. -/
private theorem exists_excluding_quotient (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ b : Fin n → Words, ¬ wordClass (prescribedValue b) (parityQuotient n) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := exists_admissible (affineSubgroup n)
  let mark (i : Fin n) : affineSubgroup n := ⟨fun x ↦ RegularWreathProduct.inl (.ofAdd (x i)),
    0, Pi.evalAddMonoidHom (fun _ : Fin n ↦ F₂) i, fun x ↦ (zero_add (x i)).symm⟩
  choose b hb using fun i ↦ hv.1 (mark i)
  let q (x : Cube n) : Epi Wreath := ⟨(coord n x).comp v, (coord_surjective n x).comp hv.1⟩
  have hwgt (x : Cube n) : swapProduct b (q x) = ∏ i, x i := by
    apply Finset.prod_congr rfl
    intro i _
    change sign (coord n x (v (b i))) = x i
    rw [hb]
    rfl
  refine ⟨b, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  let p := QuotientGroup.mk' (evenCenter n)
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := h (p.comp v) (admissible_comp hv p (QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective _))
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := realize_constraints b (t ∪ Finset.univ.image q)
  have hker := (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff (v w)).mp
    (ht w (fun f hf ↦ hw _ (Finset.mem_union_left _ hf)))
  obtain ⟨d, hd, hdw⟩ := hker
  have hd' (x : Cube n) : d x = ∏ i, x i := by
    rw [← hwgt]
    apply centralElt_injective
    exact (hdw x).symm.trans
      (hw _ (Finset.mem_union_right _ (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_univ x))))
  simp [hd', sum_coordinate_product] at hd

private theorem generated_isFormation (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] :
    IsFormation (formationGeneratedBy G) := by
  constructor
  · intro H K _ _ _ _ f hf hH F hF hG
    exact hF.1 H K f hf (hH F hF hG)
  · intro H _ _ N M _ _ hN hM F hF hG
    exact hF.2 H N M (hN F hF hG) (hM F hF hG)

private theorem refuted_of_separated_family (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G]
    (H : ℕ → Type) [∀ i, Group (H i)] [∀ i, Finite (H i)]
    (hmem : ∀ i, formationGeneratedBy G (H i))
    (hsep : ∀ i j, i < j → ¬ formationGeneratedBy (H j) (H i)) :
    ¬ finitelyManySubformations := by
  intro hf
  let formations : ℕ → FiniteGroupClass := fun i ↦ formationGeneratedBy (H i)
  have hinj : Function.Injective formations := by
    intro i j hij
    have transfer (a b : ℕ) (hab : formations a = formations b) :
        formationGeneratedBy (H b) (H a) := by
      change formations b (H a)
      rw [← hab]
      exact fun _ _ h ↦ h
    rcases lt_trichotomy i j with h | h | h
    · exact (hsep i j h (transfer i j hij)).elim
    · exact h
    · exact (hsep j i h (transfer j i hij.symm)).elim
  apply Set.infinite_of_injective_forall_mem (f := formations) hinj _ (hf G)
  intro i
  exact ⟨generated_isFormation (H i), fun K _ _ hK F hF hG ↦ hK F hF (hmem i F hF hG)⟩

/--
**The formation generated by a finite group can have infinitely many subformations.** There is
a finite group $G$ such that infinitely many formations are contained in the formation generated
by $G$. That is, the answer to Kourovka Problem 16.31 is negative, even for finite $G$.

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 16.31 (V. A.
Vedernikov); resolution: V. P. Burichenko, J. Algebra 372 (2012), 428-458, Kourovka Archive, Problem
16.31 (No, not always, even for G finite).
-/
public theorem finitelyManySubformations_refuted : ¬ finitelyManySubformations := by
  apply refuted_of_separated_family Wreath parityQuotient parityQuotient_mem
  intro i j h hmem
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := exists_excluding_quotient i
  exact hb (hmem _ (wordClass_formation _) (largerQuotient_mem b h))

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FormationSubformationsFiniteKourovka16Problem31Wanted
